     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Develop policy documents within the Justice Sector based on human rights and gender based approaches and aligned with the SDG and international human rights [Activity 1]
- Build synergies among law enforcement agencies on issues of investigation and prosecution of VE and terrorism cases [Activity 1]
- Assist national counterparts to develop policies and advocacy activities to promote human rights</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 2 national platforms of joint dialogue on judicial challenges to investigate and prosecute transnational crimes, terrorism and connected crimes involving 200 prosecutors and investigators held in February 2022 and October 2022 in Maputo and Tete Province [Activity 1]
- One Regional Dialogue of Chief Prosecutors and Chief Police Investigators held in September 2022, the first ever held in the region, convened 150 high level prosecutors and investigators and the SADC plus Uganda, Kenya, Ruanda and Nigeria. The event resulted in strengthening judicial cooperation on counterterrorism and its financing at the regional level, built capacities for joint investigation, and led to the adoption of the Maputo Declaration, a joint commitment to better respond to VE through judicial cooperation. [Activity1]
- 8 delegates from Government, CSO and NHRC participated in the Regional Dialogue on Business and Human Rights In Accra - Ghana, in a peer to peer process resulting in improved knowledge on the regional dimension of BHR and the implementation practices on the UN Guiding Principles. [Activity 3]
- 150 state and non state representatives participated in the Maputo Regional Dialogue of Southern African Region on Business and Human Rights, organized by the Ministry of Justice with the support of UNDP, UNICEF and OHCHR. The event paved the way for better dialogue among different actors on issues of BHR and provided an opportunity for Mozambique to position itself as a regional champion of the BHR Agenda [Activity 3]
- Launched the process of Development of the National Action Plan on Business and Human Rights, compliant with the commitments taken by Mozambique in the UPR III Cycle [Activity 3].</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
